# PostgreSQL Data Integrity

## Database of record

- PostgreSQL is the authoritative operational database.
- Use foreign keys for relational integrity among users, roles, tasks, approvals, and related entities.
- Multi-record business operations must use database transactions (`atomic`).

## JSONB

- PostgreSQL JSONB may store flexible checklist snapshots and answers where schema variability is justified.
- JSONB must not replace relational modeling for identities, permissions, workflow status, or audit linkage.

## History and amendments

- Do not delete submitted or approved operational records in place.
- Corrections use amendments with full before/after history.
- Soft-delete or archival patterns for operational data require explicit design approval.

## Files

- Do not store photos or large binary files in PostgreSQL.
- Store evidence in object storage (MinIO locally; S3-compatible in production) and persist metadata/references in PostgreSQL.

## Migrations

- All schema changes go through Django migrations.
- Destructive migrations require explicit review and backup awareness.
